      "writtenOn": "2024-11-11T08:06:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If your concern is about UX perspective, I agree with you. Instead of current shared pref setting, how about this?\n\n- PREFERENCE_PINNED_FORWARDING_PORTS: List of ports that user wants to keep visible in the setting activity, regardless of the state of port.\n- PREFERENCE_ACTIVE_FORWARDING_PORTS: List of ports that are active in the guest.\n- PREFERENCE_ENABLED_FORWARDING_PORTS: List of ports that are set as enabled through setting activity.\n\nSo it should be worked as:\n\n- Ports shown as enabled in the setting activity: intersect(union(ACTIVE, PINNED), ENABLED)\n- Ports shown as disabled in the setting activity: union(ACTIVE, PINNED) - ENABLED\n- Ports shown as pinned in the setting activity: PINNED\n- Ports for actual forwarding: intersect(ACTIVE, ENABLED)\n\nBut I prefer to do this in the following changes, since these are highly relying on UI side.",
